{"name":"Sultana","hex":"#674668","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Sultana","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","A census-designated place in Tulare County, California, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Sultana"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sultana (grape)","blocks":[{"text":"The sultana is a \"white\", oval seedless grape variety also called the sultanina, Thompson Seedless, Lady de Coverly (England), and oval-fruited Kishmish. It is also known as a grape found in İzmir, or Manisa in Turkey, since this variety has been extensively grown in the region around those cities. It is assumed to originate from Asia Minor, which later became part of the Ottoman Empire."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Thompson_seedless_grapes.JPG/330px-Thompson_seedless_grapes.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sultana_(grape)"},{"title":"Raisin","blocks":[{"text":"A raisin is a dried grape. Raisins are produced in many regions of the world and may be eaten raw or used in cooking, baking, and brewing. The word raisin is commonly used for the dried dark-colored seedless grape, while sultana is a golden-colored dried grape, and currant is a dried small Black Corinth seedless grape."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Raisins_01.jpg/330px-Raisins_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raisin"},{"title":"Sultana (steamboat)","blocks":[{"text":"Sultana was a commercial side-wheel steamboat which exploded and sank on the Mississippi River on April 27, 1865, killing 1,164 people in what remains the worst maritime disaster in United States history."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Ill-fated_Sultana%2C_Helena%2C_Arkansas%2C_April_27%2C_1865.jpg/330px-Ill-fated_Sultana%2C_Helena%2C_Arkansas%2C_April_27%2C_1865.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sultana_(steamboat)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Raisins_2.jpg/500px-Raisins_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Raisins_2.jpg/500px-Raisins_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARaisins_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Sultanas2.JPG/500px-Sultanas2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Sultanas2.JPG/1280px-Sultanas2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Sultanas2.JPG/500px-Sultanas2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASultanas2.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Grape_Rasins_plus_Zante_Currants.jpg/500px-Grape_Rasins_plus_Zante_Currants.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Grape_Rasins_plus_Zante_Currants.jpg/1280px-Grape_Rasins_plus_Zante_Currants.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Grape_Rasins_plus_Zante_Currants.jpg/500px-Grape_Rasins_plus_Zante_Currants.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"California seedless grape raisins (left) and California Zante currants","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrape_Rasins_plus_Zante_Currants.jpg"},{"srcset":"h